 # Point Cloud Voxelization
-Also called: 3D Point Cloud Voxelization (NumPy), Basic NumPy version, Numba-friendly JIT version, VoxelGrid Contains, Voxelization from Point Cloud, contains, voxelize
+Also called: Voxelization from Point Cloud
 
 ## Overview
-Point Cloud Voxelization converts a continuous 3D point cloud into a discrete, sparse voxel grid by mapping each point to a grid cell and aggregating data within occupied cells [S2, S3, unofficial]. Unlike mesh-based voxelization which determines occupancy via geometric intersection, this method relies on direct coordinate projection, making it suitable for unstructured point data [S2]. It is distinguished from [3D Grid Rasterization](903-3d-grid-rasterization.md) by its handling of multiple points per voxel (aggregation) rather than binary occupancy, and from [Voxel Occupancy Test](1281-voxel-occupancy-test.md) by its construction of the full data structure rather than a simple boolean query [S2, S3, unofficial].
+Point Cloud Voxelization converts a continuous 3D point cloud into a discrete, sparse voxel grid by mapping each point to a grid cell and aggregating data within occupied cells [S2, S3, unofficial]. Unlike mesh-based voxelization which determines occupancy via geometric intersection, this method relies on direct coordinate projection, making it suitable for unstructured point data [S2].
 
